{
  "uid": "sandbox-signals",
  "title": "Repro / Bug Signals",
  "description": "The bug-hunting board. Mixes SDK and server metrics to surface non-determinism, workflow task retries, sticky cache behaviour, replay pressure, and injected faults. This is the one with no upstream equivalent.",
  "tags": [
    "sandbox",
    "signals"
  ],
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "time": {
    "from": "now-30m",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "refresh": "10s",
  "timezone": "browser",
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "namespace",
        "label": "SDK namespace",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "sandbox-prometheus"
        },
        "query": "label_values(temporal_request{service_name=\"temporal-core-sdk\"}, namespace)",
        "refresh": 1,
        "includeAll": false,
        "multi": false,
        "current": {
          "text": "default",
          "value": "default",
          "selected": true
        },
        "description": "Values are NOT sanitized by the .NET SDK; dashes survive."
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Non-determinism failures (dashboard range)",
      "description": "The number to look at first when a repro involves changed workflow code. Uses increase() over the range, not rate(), so short runs still register. failure_reason=\"NonDeterminismError\" is the identical string in Core and Go -- verified in sdk-core's FailureReason Display impl, not assumed.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "sandbox-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(increase(temporal_workflow_task_execution_failed{namespace=\"$namespace\",service_name=\"temporal-core-sdk\",failure_reason=\"NonDeterminismError\"}[$__range])) or vector(0)",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "sandbox-prometheus"
          },
          "legendFormat": "non-determinism"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Server-side non-determinism /s",
      "description": "The server's independent count. Should move with the SDK's.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "sandbox-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 0
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(rate(service_errors_nondeterministic[$__rate_interval])) or vector(0)",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "sandbox-prometheus"
          },
          "legendFormat": "server view"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Workflow task attempt p99",
      "description": "Above 1 means workflow tasks are being retried -- a stuck workflow rather than a slow one.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "sandbox-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 0
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(workflow_task_attempt_bucket[$__rate_interval])))",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "sandbox-prometheus"
          },
          "legendFormat": "p99 attempt"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {}
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "textMode": "auto",
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "area"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Schedule-to-start: SDK view vs server view",
      "description": "Two independent measurements of the SAME quantity: how long a WORKFLOW task sat between being scheduled and being started. They should track each other closely; sustained divergence means clock skew or dispatch loss.\n\nTHE * 1000 IS NOT DECORATION. Core records milliseconds; the server's tally timers record seconds. Plotting them raw puts a 1000x gap on the panel that looks exactly like the dispatch loss this panel exists to detect. The Go original needed no conversion because both sides were seconds.\n\nTHE task_type PIN IS NOT DECORATION EITHER. The SDK metric is workflow-task-only by construction (activities have their own temporal_activity_schedule_to_start_latency), but the server's task_schedule_to_start_latency_bucket is one histogram carrying both task_type=\"Workflow\" and task_type=\"Activity\". Sum over it and the two lines are not the same quantity, so every gap between them reads as divergence when it is really just the activity half of a different metric.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "sandbox-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(temporal_workflow_task_schedule_to_start_latency_bucket{namespace=\"$namespace\",service_name=\"temporal-core-sdk\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "sandbox-prometheus"
          },
          "legendFormat": "SDK (worker), ms"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "1000 * histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(task_schedule_to_start_latency_bucket{service_name=\"history\",task_type=\"Workflow\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "sandbox-prometheus"
          },
          "legendFormat": "SERVER (history), s -> ms"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ms",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            }
          },
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ],
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Workflow task failures by reason",
      "description": "Core's failure_reason vocabulary, read from the source rather than the docs: NonDeterminismError, WorkflowError, ActivityError, timeout, GrpcMessageTooLarge, PayloadsTooLarge, ExternalStorageError, RequestTooLarge, plus operation_<name> and handler_error_<name> for Nexus.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "sandbox-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 14
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (failure_reason) (rate(temporal_workflow_task_execution_failed{namespace=\"$namespace\",service_name=\"temporal-core-sdk\"}[$__rate_interval])) or vector(0)",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "sandbox-prometheus"
          },
          "legendFormat": "{{failure_reason}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 40,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "normal",
              "group": "A"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ],
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Replay latency p95",
      "description": "Time spent replaying history to rebuild workflow state. Grows with history length when the sticky cache misses. Shares Core's [1..1000] ms bucket set with workflow task execution latency, so no override is needed.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "sandbox-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 14
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(temporal_workflow_task_replay_latency_bucket{namespace=\"$namespace\",service_name=\"temporal-core-sdk\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "sandbox-prometheus"
          },
          "legendFormat": "p95"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ms",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            }
          },
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ],
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Sticky cache hit ratio",
      "description": "A REAL hit ratio, and the clearest win in the whole Go -> .NET port. Go+tally emits no sticky_cache_miss metric, so the original board could only ship an approximation (hits divided by workflow task executions) with a paragraph apologising for it. Core emits temporal_sticky_cache_miss, so this is hit / (hit + miss) -- the actual quantity.\n\nFalling toward 0 means workers keep rebuilding state from history instead of resuming from cache. Look at forced evictions and MaxCachedWorkflows next.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "sandbox-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 22
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "(sum(rate(temporal_sticky_cache_hit{namespace=\"$namespace\",service_name=\"temporal-core-sdk\"}[$__rate_interval])) or vector(0)) / clamp_min((sum(rate(temporal_sticky_cache_hit{namespace=\"$namespace\",service_name=\"temporal-core-sdk\"}[$__rate_interval])) or vector(0)) + (sum(rate(temporal_sticky_cache_miss{namespace=\"$namespace\",service_name=\"temporal-core-sdk\"}[$__rate_interval])) or vector(0)), 1e-9)",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "sandbox-prometheus"
          },
          "legendFormat": "hit ratio"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            }
          },
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ],
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Sticky cache hits and misses /s",
      "description": "The two series behind the ratio. A miss is a workflow task that arrived for a workflow this worker no longer had cached -- it had to fetch and replay history to answer it.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "sandbox-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 22
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(rate(temporal_sticky_cache_hit{namespace=\"$namespace\",service_name=\"temporal-core-sdk\"}[$__rate_interval])) or vector(0)",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "sandbox-prometheus"
          },
          "legendFormat": "hits/s"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "sum(rate(temporal_sticky_cache_miss{namespace=\"$namespace\",service_name=\"temporal-core-sdk\"}[$__rate_interval])) or vector(0)",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "sandbox-prometheus"
          },
          "legendFormat": "misses/s"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ],
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Cached workflows and forced evictions",
      "description": "Forced evictions are the leading indicator of replay storms. Note temporal_sticky_cache_total_forced_eviction keeps its 'total' -- that is part of the metric NAME in Core, not the _total counter suffix, so it survives the suffix change.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "sandbox-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 30
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(temporal_sticky_cache_size{namespace=\"$namespace\",service_name=\"temporal-core-sdk\"})",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "sandbox-prometheus"
          },
          "legendFormat": "cached workflows"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "sum(rate(temporal_sticky_cache_total_forced_eviction{namespace=\"$namespace\",service_name=\"temporal-core-sdk\"}[$__rate_interval])) or vector(0)",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "sandbox-prometheus"
          },
          "legendFormat": "forced evictions/s"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            }
          },
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ],
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Replay pressure ratio",
      "description": "Replayed workflow tasks over executed workflow tasks. Directional proxy, not an exact quantity: toward 1.0 means most tasks are rebuilding state instead of resuming from cache. Now that a real hit ratio exists two panels up, treat this as corroboration.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "sandbox-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 30
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "(sum(rate(temporal_workflow_task_replay_latency_count{namespace=\"$namespace\",service_name=\"temporal-core-sdk\"}[$__rate_interval])) or vector(0)) / clamp_min(sum(rate(temporal_workflow_task_execution_latency_count{namespace=\"$namespace\",service_name=\"temporal-core-sdk\"}[$__rate_interval])), 1e-9)",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "sandbox-prometheus"
          },
          "legendFormat": "replay/exec"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            }
          },
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ],
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 11,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Activity retried but recovered /s",
      "description": "activity_task_fail counts every failed attempt; activity_fail counts only terminal failures. The difference is work the retry policy rescued. Raise fault.failureRate to make this move.\n\nThe third series is the SDK's own per-attempt failure count. Go's equivalent (temporal_activity_task_error) does not exist in Core; temporal_activity_execution_failed does, and it should track activity_task_fail one-for-one. If it does not, the worker is failing activities the server never hears about.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "sandbox-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 38
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "(sum(rate(activity_task_fail{namespace=\"default\"}[$__rate_interval])) or vector(0)) - (sum(rate(activity_fail{namespace=\"default\"}[$__rate_interval])) or vector(0))",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "sandbox-prometheus"
          },
          "legendFormat": "recovered/s (server)"
        },
        {
          "refId": "B",
          "expr": "sum by (activity_type) (rate(temporal_activity_execution_failed{namespace=\"$namespace\",service_name=\"temporal-core-sdk\"}[$__rate_interval])) or vector(0)",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "sandbox-prometheus"
          },
          "legendFormat": "{{activity_type}} failed attempts/s (SDK)"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ],
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Custom: repro workflow outcomes /s",
      "description": "Emitted from Workflow.MetricMeter. Replay-suppressed with NO opt-out -- ReplaySafeMetricMeter is internal in the .NET SDK, exactly as in Go. Custom metric names are NOT prefixed with MetricPrefix, so this is a literal `repro_` and there is no `temporal_` in front of it.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "sandbox-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 38
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum by (outcome) (rate(repro_workflow_completed{namespace=\"$namespace\",service_name=\"temporal-core-sdk\"}[$__rate_interval])) or vector(0)",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "sandbox-prometheus"
          },
          "legendFormat": "{{outcome}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 40,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "normal",
              "group": "A"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ],
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Custom: repro workflow latency p95 by outcome",
      "description": "Recorded with CreateHistogram<TimeSpan>, which follows UseSecondsForDuration automatically -- so milliseconds, and no unit suffix on the name. Custom histograms fall into Core's catch-all bucket set [50, 100, 500, 1000, 2500, 10000] ms, which tops out at 10 s. The seed heartbeating workflow runs longer than that, so this one REQUIRES a HistogramBucketOverrides entry too.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "sandbox-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 46
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le, outcome) (rate(repro_workflow_latency_bucket{namespace=\"$namespace\",service_name=\"temporal-core-sdk\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "sandbox-prometheus"
          },
          "legendFormat": "{{outcome}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "ms",
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 10,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            }
          },
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "table",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull",
            "max"
          ],
          "showLegend": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Custom: injected activity faults",
      "description": "Direct view of the fault injector. Both series stay at 0 until fault.failureRate is raised in config.yaml.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "sandbox-prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 46
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(rate(repro_activity_failed{namespace=\"$namespace\",service_name=\"temporal-core-sdk\"}[$__rate_interval])) or vector(0)",
          "datasource": {
